            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous reversal of flow through jeopardized collateral vessels during non-Q wave myocardial infarction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>103-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This case report documents that, when a severely diseased donor artery occludes, sufficient spontaneous reversal of flow through the collaterals can occur to prevent an extensive and possibly fatal transmural infarction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
